## 🔀 Git & Development Conventions

### Branch Naming

- **PATTERN**: `feature/[description]`, `fix/[description]`, `refactor/[description]`
- **EXAMPLES**: `feature/doctor-search`, `fix/booking-validation`, `refactor/auth-forms`
- **FORBIDDEN**: Generic names like `fix-bug`, `update`, `wip`

### Commit Message Format

Use **Conventional Commits** format: `type(scope): description`

- `feat(auth): add sign-in validation`
- `fix(booking): resolve date picker timezone issue`
- `refactor(design-system): migrate Button to design tokens`
- `chore(deps): update RTK Query to v2`

Types: `feat`, `fix`, `refactor`, `chore`, `docs`, `test`, `perf`

### Code Review Standards

All code changes require review. Reviewers must verify:

- [ ] Follows TypeScript strict mode (no `any`, no unsafe casting)
- [ ] Uses design system components (no direct RN components in features)
- [ ] No inline styles — all styles in separate `.styles.ts` files
- [ ] No hardcoded style values — all tokens from design system
- [ ] Proper error handling with user-friendly messages
- [ ] Loading and empty states implemented
- [ ] Follows naming conventions
- [ ] `yarn verify` passes with zero errors/warnings

