## 🎯 Success Criteria

Every change must:

- ✅ Follow established architectural patterns
- ✅ Use design system components exclusively
- ✅ **ALL styles derive from design tokens (zero hardcoded values)**
- ✅ Implement proper TypeScript typing (strict, no `any`)
- ✅ Include loading and empty states
- ✅ Handle errors gracefully with user-friendly messaging
- ✅ Follow naming conventions
- ✅ Maintain code organization standards
- ✅ Keep business logic separated from UI rendering
- ✅ Be production-ready (not demo-quality)
- ✅ Be easy to refactor and extend
- ✅ Meet UI/UX industry standards (WCAG 2.1 AA, touch targets, interaction feedback)
- ✅ Meet React Native performance standards (no unnecessary re-renders, optimized lists, performant animations)

---

**Remember**: The goal is consistency, maintainability, excellent user experience, and production-grade quality. When in doubt, reference existing patterns in the codebase. Always think and respond as a senior reviewer who cares deeply about long-term scalability.
